      "writtenOn": "2019-01-08T16:27:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you Hyuanwoo and Aaron for the explanation. Since this is a single core, \"lock\" does not have any effect. I can safely remove it here and in atomic.h\n\nI would however like to keep the lock statement here (and in atomic.h) since 1) it would be safer for multi-core situations (which may be a scenario that never happens though) and 2) I think it documents the code a little better because it makes the reader understand that __in_isr is a global var that multiple reader and writers access. Hopefully the cost of keeping it on a single core chip is negligible, since there is no other core to notify during \"the lock part\" of the operation.\n\nEither way, I will update this and atomic.h to be the same. Hyungwoo and Aaron, are you still against leaving the \"lock\" with the above justification?",
      "parentUuid": "3db4acfc_7f84f60e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 49,
        "startChar": 4,
